+      <t indent="0" pn="section-2.0-1">The Aggregatable Global Unicast Address Allocation format defined in <xref target="AGGR" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="AGGR"/> is as follows:</t>
+      <artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt="" pn="section-2.0-2"><![CDATA[
+      | 3 |  13 |    32     |   16   |          64 bits               |
+      +---+-----+-----------+--------+--------------------------------+
+      |FP | TLA | NLA ID    | SLA ID |         Interface ID           |
+      |   | ID  |           |        |                                |
+      +---+-----+-----------+--------+--------------------------------+
 ]]></artwork>
-</t>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-2.0-5"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-        This is the Format Prefix used to identify aggregatable
-        global unicast addresses.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-2.0-6"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   TLA = 0x1FFE = Top-Level Aggregation Identifier
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-2.0-7"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
